{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_android", "label": "Android build, install and instrumentation checks", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_ios", "label": "iOS build, simulator test and device link checks", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_toolchain", "label": "Pinned toolchain selection (Rust 1.100.0, UniFFI 0.31.2, Xcode, AGP 9.1.0)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L103", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_hello_world_greeting", "label": "Hello, World! greeting shown by SwiftUI and Compose apps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_uniffi", "label": "UniFFI 0.31.2 (runtime and host binding generator)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L107", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_shared_build_and_generation", "label": "Shared build and generation commands", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme", "label": "README: Native mobile foundation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_start_a_project_from_this_foundation", "label": "Start a project from this foundation (clone at a foundation-v tag, keep the foundation as a second remote, run scripts/init-project.sh --name --app-id)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A product changes only its display name, application ID and version. Every other name stays as the foundation wrote it (Xcode project, crates, Kotlin packages, generated types), which is what lets a later foundation release arrive by an ordinary merge. Cloning a tag leaves no branch checked out, which is why the branch is created first."}, {"id": "readme_init_command_behavior", "label": "init-project.sh behavior: needs a clean tree; writes name, ID, version 0.1.0 and build 1 into both identity files, the README title and origin line, an empty verification record, and removes graphify-out/; renames nothing, changes no git state; refusals exit 2 with nothing written", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_finish_the_start_by_hand", "label": "Finish the start by hand: rebuild the knowledge graph (/graphify .), mark inherited scope rows existing (/scope), commit, run scripts/test.sh and both native builds, push, record the first local and hosted results", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_init_project_check", "label": "scripts/init-project.sh --check: prints foundation or derived; exits 1 and names each mismatch when a checkout is in between; scripts/test.sh runs it on every change", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "To change the name, ID or version later, edit the two identity files. If the command stops part way, git restore . returns the checkout to the foundation state."}, {"id": "readme_who_owns_which_path", "label": "Who owns which path: the product keeps its side (identity files, docs/scope, docs/specs, verification record, graphify-out, README title and origin line); the foundation's side is taken (scripts, tooling, workflow, schemas, toolchain pins, Xcode project file, Gradle build files); shared paths merge by hand", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fix to foundation owned paths is made in the foundation and arrives by merge."}, {"id": "readme_take_a_later_foundation_release", "label": "Take a later foundation release (git fetch foundation --tags, git merge foundation-vX.Y.Z, keep the product's side on product owned paths)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every such merge reports conflicts on the paths the product owns, because the foundation changes its own graph, scope and verification record in most commits. The origin line is not changed: it records where the product started, and git log --merges shows each release taken since. These merge steps have not been exercised yet; the first release merged into a product will prove them."}, {"id": "readme_release_the_foundation", "label": "Release the foundation (foundation repository only): run the workflow by hand with derived set, then create and push an annotated tag foundation-vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH on main", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both native jobs derive the runner checkout and build and test both apps under a sample identity before a tag is cut. A product never creates a tag that starts with foundation-v."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme", "target": "agents", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confi